      "lines": 1,
      "align": "left",
      "style": "object",
      "text": {
        "en": "Seven-Point Star Mirror",
        "zh": "七角星纹铜镜"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "caption.01",
      "bay": 1,
      "label": "CAPTION 01 · 40–60 WORDS / ≤4 LINES",
      "x": 4.35,
      "y": 1.59,
      "w": 1.7,
      "h": 0.3,
      "words": 60,
      "lines": 4,
      "align": "left",
      "style": "caption",
      "text": {
        "en": "Cast by the Qijia culture of the upper Yellow River, this small bronze disc is among the earliest mirrors known in China. Its back carries a seven-point star around a pierced knob, while one face was polished to hold a reflection. Such mirrors accompanied the dead, tying early metallurgy to beliefs about light and the soul.",
        "zh": "此镜铸造于黄河上游的齐家文化时期，是中国已知最早的铜镜之一。镜背以穿孔镜钮为中心饰七角星纹，镜面则打磨光亮以照容。此类铜镜多随葬于墓中，将早期冶铸技术与古人关于光明、灵魂的信仰联系在一起。"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "meta.01",
      "bay": 1,
      "label": "DATE / MEDIUM / LENDER",
      "x": 4.35,
      "y": 1.44,
      "w": 1.7,
      "h": 0.07,
      "lines": 1,
      "align": "left",
      "style": "meta",
      "text": {
        "en": "c. 2000 BC · Bronze · Guinan, Qinghai",
        "zh": "约公元前2000年 · 青铜 · 青海贵南"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "section.02",
      "bay": 2,
