    },
    {
      "id": "caption.04",
      "bay": 4,
      "label": "CAPTION 05 · 40–60 WORDS / ≤4 LINES",
      "x": 10.35,
      "y": 1.59,
      "w": 1.7,
      "h": 0.3,
      "words": 60,
      "lines": 4,
      "align": "left",
      "style": "caption",
      "text": {
        "en": "Excavated in 2002 from the Tang tomb of Yan Zhi and his wife at Majiagou, Baqiao, Xi'an, this eight-lobed mirror is a masterpiece of gold-backed casting. Its repoussé gold shell shows eight beasts among scrolling vines, grapes and birds spilling across the lobes — Central Asian motifs meeting Chinese craft on the Silk Road.",
        "zh": "2002年出土于西安灞桥马家沟唐代阎智与夫人裴氏合葬墓。镜作八出菱花形，背贴锤揲金壳：内区八只瑞兽攀枝嬉戏，外区葡萄藤蔓与禽鸟过梁缠绕，是丝绸之路将西域葡萄纹与中原铸镜工艺融于一镜的巅峰之作。"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "meta.04",
      "bay": 4,
