      "lines": 4,
      "align": "left",
      "style": "caption",
      "text": {
        "en": "From the British Museum collection, this Song-dynasty bronze mirror is cast with a deity mounted on a deer amid clouds and waves, a long handle extending from the rim so it could be held or hung. Turn it in the viewer to follow the rider across the lively, crowded ground of the back.",
        "zh": "此镜为大英博物馆藏宋代铜镜，镜背铸仙人骑鹿、云气涌动，镜缘伸出长柄，可执可悬。请在观赏器中缓缓转动，跟随骑鹿仙人穿行于繁密生动的纹饰之间。"
      }
    },
